WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:06.640
Okay, moving on to the next scenario to the next use case.

00:06.640 --> 00:12.280
We use SQL views in order to implement security and to protect our data in the database.

00:12.280 --> 00:17.720
In many scenarios, we have sensitive informations in our data and we cannot go and share it with everyone.

00:17.720 --> 00:24.040
So one of the best practices is to create views in order to protect your data before sharing it with

00:24.040 --> 00:24.800
the users.

00:24.800 --> 00:26.440
So let's understand what this means.

00:26.440 --> 00:30.520
So now let's understand first the scenario without views only tables.

00:30.520 --> 00:33.960
So now let's say that you have the table orders four columns and three rows.

00:34.000 --> 00:39.000
And then you have like for example, a manager that has an access directly to the database and start

00:39.000 --> 00:41.320
writing some queries in order to retrieve data.

00:41.320 --> 00:46.400
But in your project you have multiple people that has an access to your database, like for example,

00:46.440 --> 00:47.320
a data analyst.

00:47.320 --> 00:51.080
And as well she is writing a script in order to retrieve data from the orders.

00:51.080 --> 00:56.360
And as well, you have maybe a student that has an access to your database and querying the data like

00:56.360 --> 00:58.680
any other rule, like a manager and data analyst.

00:58.680 --> 01:04.680
So as you can see, you have now different rules in your project and all of them having the same rights

01:04.680 --> 01:06.800
by accessing directly your table.

01:06.850 --> 01:13.530
So a manager or a data analyst or a student, they are seeing the whole table or rows and all columns.

01:13.530 --> 01:16.570
And of course in the real projects this is a big problem.

01:16.570 --> 01:20.730
Sometimes the data are sensitive and you cannot give an access for everyone.

01:20.730 --> 01:24.730
And of course if you are using only tables, this is going to be a nightmare because you can go and

01:24.730 --> 01:29.210
create multiple tables, but it's going to be really hard to make all those tables in sync.

01:29.210 --> 01:31.490
But instead of that, we have views.

01:31.490 --> 01:37.210
So what you can do, you can go and remove all accesses to the physical table, but instead you can

01:37.210 --> 01:40.450
go and create multiple views for each role.

01:40.450 --> 01:44.090
For example, you can go and create a view called orders Managers.

01:44.090 --> 01:49.250
And maybe you can give all the data and all the columns because the managers are allowed to see, let's

01:49.250 --> 01:50.330
say, sensitive data.

01:50.330 --> 01:52.010
But still it's nice to create a view.

01:52.050 --> 01:54.930
Maybe you change your mind later and you go and remove something.

01:54.970 --> 01:59.890
Now let's say that for the data analyst, you want to offer all the data, but there is only one column

01:59.890 --> 02:01.530
that is very sensitive.

02:01.530 --> 02:05.530
So what you can do, you can go and create another view called orders Analyst.

02:05.530 --> 02:11.610
So in the view only three columns are available A, B, C and then you give access to all data analyst.

02:11.610 --> 02:15.070
And with that you have protected this sensitive information.

02:15.070 --> 02:17.390
So we call this column level security.

02:17.390 --> 02:19.310
And now we come to our poor students.

02:19.510 --> 02:25.910
And here we create another view where we are not only protecting the column D, but also we are protecting

02:25.950 --> 02:31.350
few rows like for example, the row number three because we want to offer only few informations to the

02:31.350 --> 02:32.030
students.

02:32.030 --> 02:35.030
So we are protecting the columns and as well the rows.

02:35.070 --> 02:40.350
And for that we can create another dedicated view called for example order students and we can offer

02:40.350 --> 02:41.270
it to the students.

02:41.270 --> 02:46.390
And with that we are doing column level security and as well row level security.

02:46.390 --> 02:52.630
So we are offering multiple views very easily without having to worry how to load the data from one

02:52.630 --> 02:53.670
table to another.

02:53.670 --> 03:00.430
So creating those views are really easy and provide us a perfect tool in order to manage the security

03:00.430 --> 03:01.350
of our data.

03:01.350 --> 03:05.830
So this is one very common use case of using views in data projects.

03:05.870 --> 03:06.150
All right.

03:06.150 --> 03:07.510
So now let's have the following task.

03:07.510 --> 03:14.790
And it says provide a view for a new sales team that combines details from all tables and excludes data

03:14.790 --> 03:16.190
related to the USA.

03:16.430 --> 03:22.120
So the first part of the task is similar to what we have already done, but we cannot offer all data

03:22.120 --> 03:23.240
for the user.

03:23.240 --> 03:28.800
So this time we are providing a view that is specifically created for a team, the sales team.

03:28.800 --> 03:32.960
So the first part, we have already done it where we are combining all details in one view.

03:32.960 --> 03:37.000
But the problem with the view that we have created that it shows all data.

03:37.000 --> 03:38.360
But now the requirement change.

03:38.360 --> 03:39.880
We cannot show all data.

03:39.880 --> 03:43.720
We have to go and exclude the USA data from our details.

03:43.720 --> 03:45.000
So let's see how we can do that.

03:45.000 --> 03:45.680
It's very simple.

03:45.680 --> 03:47.240
We're going to go and grab the semi query.

03:47.320 --> 03:48.520
We'll not repeat that.

03:48.520 --> 03:52.400
So we have as well here joining tables and prepare everything.

03:52.760 --> 03:57.960
But instead of showing all data what we're going to do, we're going to go and filter the data based

03:57.960 --> 03:59.560
on the customer country.

03:59.560 --> 04:00.760
So it's very simple.

04:00.800 --> 04:09.440
At the end we will have a where clause where the see country is not equal to USA.

04:10.600 --> 04:12.960
So we have now a filter.

04:12.960 --> 04:14.160
Let's go and execute it.

04:14.160 --> 04:19.280
And with that as you can see in the output, we are getting the orders that are not from USA.

04:19.320 --> 04:22.640
And with that we are protecting the data of the USA and the EU.

04:23.080 --> 04:27.740
Sales teams can access only their data so it looks nice and protected.

04:27.740 --> 04:30.380
And with that, we are doing now row level security.

04:30.380 --> 04:36.580
That means we are hiding now all the orders, all the rows that are not allowed to be seen and consumed

04:36.580 --> 04:38.180
from this group of users.

04:38.180 --> 04:39.340
So now what is the next step?

04:39.340 --> 04:40.100
It is very simple.

04:40.100 --> 04:42.740
We're going to go and put everything in one view.

04:42.740 --> 04:46.460
So with that we have the query ready and we can go and create the new view.

04:46.780 --> 04:49.980
So we're going to call it create view.

04:50.500 --> 04:51.860
Then we need the schema.

04:52.340 --> 04:54.740
And the name going to be almost the same.

04:54.740 --> 04:57.260
So order details but EU.

04:57.300 --> 05:01.020
And then we have to have us and parentheses like this.

05:01.500 --> 05:02.860
So everything is ready.

05:02.860 --> 05:04.100
Let's go and execute it.

05:04.140 --> 05:07.460
And now we can go and refresh in order to see our new view.

05:07.460 --> 05:12.460
If you still don't see it, you can go to the views over here and refresh as well to the folder.

05:12.460 --> 05:15.180
So with that I can see we have our new view.

05:15.220 --> 05:17.700
Now of course the next step we go and test it.

05:17.700 --> 05:27.500
So let's create a new query, select star from sales and the Order Details view.

05:27.940 --> 05:29.220
So let's test it.

05:29.220 --> 05:34.270
And with that as you can see, we are getting the combined view only for the data that is relevant for

05:34.270 --> 05:35.510
the EU sales team.

05:35.510 --> 05:38.630
So I'm not seeing here any USA records.

05:38.630 --> 05:43.750
So with that we are providing view that protects few rows like the orders from USA.

05:43.790 --> 05:49.630
So as you can see, views are really great in order to provide security to our data, whether we are

05:49.630 --> 05:55.310
protecting the columns or the rows, for example, in our view we can say not only I want to remove

05:55.430 --> 06:00.670
the USA orders, but let's say that department information is sensitive information and I would like

06:00.670 --> 06:01.790
to hide it from the view.

06:01.790 --> 06:04.270
So you can just simply remove it from the select.

06:04.270 --> 06:06.470
And with that you are doing column level security.

06:06.470 --> 06:09.470
So now I have two options that I can provide to the users.

06:09.470 --> 06:12.670
The first option doesn't have any like row level security.

06:12.710 --> 06:15.510
It is the first view the order details.

06:15.510 --> 06:16.910
We don't have there any filter.

06:16.910 --> 06:18.470
So it's going to show all the orders.

06:18.470 --> 06:21.990
So here we give access only to people that are allowed to see all data.

06:21.990 --> 06:23.950
And we have another option the details.

06:23.950 --> 06:26.230
With the EU it doesn't show all data.

06:26.230 --> 06:29.630
It shows only a subset that is relevant for the EU team.

06:29.630 --> 06:34.190
So now it's really easy to control the security of my data using the views.

06:34.190 --> 06:36.750
And this is very important use case for the views.
